The cutover from EXAMTRAC to SENTRY completed over the weekend of March 5 a=
nd 6. EXAMTRAC is now read-only and will be decommissioned at the end of th=
e fiscal year. All new examination records go into SENTRY.<br />
<br />
Please read the migration scope notice attached before you go looking for a=
n old file, because not everything came across.<br />
<br />
In summary: for examinations closed on or after January 1, 2014, the full r=
ecord migrated - summary, correspondence, work papers, exhibits and attachm=
ents. For examinations closed before January 1, 2014, only the examination =
summary record and the final letters issued to the registrant migrated. Cor=
respondence with registrants, staff call memoranda, work papers, internal r=
eview memoranda and follow-up flags for those examinations were out of scop=
e and were not migrated.<br />
<br />
Nothing has been deleted. The EXAMTRAC data remains on the retired platform=
 pending disposition instructions, and a restore request can be raised thro=
ugh the service desk. It is not, however, searchable from SENTRY and it is =
not something you should assume is one click away.<br />
<br />
Marcus Ellenbogen<br />
Office of Information Technology
